+	/*
+	 * The same four refusals the chain below applies, in the same order --
+	 * and the refusals matter as much as the mitigation. This SoC hits the
+	 * first one: its firmware reports PSCI v0.2, so SMCCC 1.1 is never
+	 * negotiated, ARM_SMCCC_ARCH_WORKAROUND_1 does not exist, and a
+	 * Cortex-A72 (no CSV2) is therefore Spectre-v2 vulnerable with nothing
+	 * the kernel can do about it. Upstream then declines BHB as well --
+	 * "no point mitigating Spectre-BHB alone" -- and the A72 will leave
+	 * spectre_bhb_state at SPECTRE_VULNERABLE.
